course: dictionary
lesson: 4878
title: Identify: recognise, find, or share a feeling
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word identify has three main meanings, and the sentence around it tells you which one to use. When you identify something, you recognise it and can say what it is. «Pick only berries a grown-up has identified» means a grown-up has checked the berry and knows what it is, so it is safe to eat.
explain: To identify can also mean to find or pick out something, such as a pattern, a mistake or a problem. «Some apps identify birds from their songs» means the app picks out the bird from its sound. The clue here is that the app «can guess the wrong bird», so picking something out does not always mean you are right.
explain: When identify is followed by with, as in identify with, it means you understand someone's feelings and share them. If you read a story about a child who feels left out and you think, I have felt like that too, you identify with that child. Check the words after identify to find out which meaning the writer means.
explain: Use the swap test. Put a simple word into the sentence, such as «recognise» or «find», and see if it still makes sense. «Geologists identify minerals by hardness, colour, lustre (shine), streak and how they break» works with «recognise» because geologists recognise minerals by their features.
fact: Identify means to recognise and say who or what someone or something is.
fact: Identify also means to find or pick out something, such as a pattern, a mistake or a problem.
fact: Identify with someone means you feel that you understand them or share their feelings.
fact: «Pick only berries a grown-up has identified» means only eat berries that a grown-up knows are safe.
fact: «Some apps identify birds from their songs», but they can guess the wrong bird, so check with a person who knows birds.
exercise: «Pick only berries a grown-up has identified.» What does identified mean here? | Eaten quickly | *Recognised and said what they are | Thrown away | Picked from a tree
exercise: In maths you can identify a pattern in numbers. What does that mean? | To write the numbers bigger | *To find and pick out the pattern | To rub out a number | To add all the numbers in a list
exercise: Ella says she can identify with a character who feels left out. What does identify with mean? | *To understand their feelings and share them | To take the character's book away | To draw a picture of the character | To say the character's name
test: «Geologists identify minerals by hardness, colour, lustre and streak.» What do geologists do? | Make minerals into jewellery | Dig holes to find water | Paint pictures of rocks | *Recognise minerals by their features
test: «Some apps identify birds from their songs», but they can guess the... What might an app get wrong? | The colour of the sky | *The wrong bird | The time of day | Its own name
exam: «Everyone except identical twins has slightly different DNA, so a sample can identify a person.» What does identify mean here? | Hide a person | Forget a person | Pay a person | *Recognise who a person is
